       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and normal kidney function doesn't make them safe.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max dose.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** That could be 850 mg twice daily, or about 567 mg three times daily, which isn't a standard tablet strength.\n- **Another dose.** For example, a starting dose of 500 mg twice daily or 500 mg three times daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give me a note for the order. I'd advise against it."
      }
